# Post-deploy smoke test (Railway staging)

After every deploy to staging or when the user mentions Railway/production issues:

1. Wait **at least 120 seconds** after push for Railway to fully deploy (`pnpm run smoke:staging` does this automatically).
2. Run `pnpm run smoke:staging` against https://eggrollpos-staging.up.railway.app/
3. If merchant/menu checks are skipped, ask for or use Railway env vars `STAGING_MERCHANT_KEY` and `STAGING_MENU_SLUG` from the staging database.
4. Treat **JS bundle returning text/html** as a production asset-path regression (see `src/server/lib/viteAssets.js`).
5. Do not assume seed routes (`mc_m4zun00d`, `instep-cafe-...`) exist on staging unless seeds were run.
6. Summarize failures with the failing URL and HTTP status/content-type.

